From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:56:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: emit a geometry shader's own clip and cull distances

A geometry shader copies TGSI's CLIPDIST outputs into clip_dist_temp and
the translator publishes them into gl_ClipDistance and gl_CullDistance
just before each EmitVertex().  That publication was conditional on
key->gs.emit_clip_distance, which vrend_renderer sets from the
rasterizer's clip_plane_enable mask, so a draw with no user clip plane
enabled produced a geometry shader that declared out float
gl_CullDistance[N], filled clip_dist_temp and emitted the vertex without
ever copying one into the other.  Every cull distance the host saw was
undefined, so nothing was culled.

The key only decides whether the legacy user clip planes have to be
evaluated in this stage, and that code inside emit_clip_dist_movs()
already applies solely to a shader that declares no clip or cull
distance of its own.  Publish the shader's own distances whenever it has
any: gl_CullDistance culls with no enable of its own, and a fragment
shader may read either array back.

KHR-GLES3.cull_distance.functional_test_item_5_primitive_mode_{points,
lines,triangles}_max_culldist_0 failed with "Primitive number [N] should
be culled by distance [0] but primitive vertex at (x,y) is visible".
Item 5 is the only functional item that routes the distances through a
passthrough geometry shader, and iteration 0 is the only one that asks
for cull distances without any clip distance, so it is the only one that
leaves clip_plane_enable at zero.  The same items pass at every other
iteration and on a desktop GL 4.6 context for the same reason.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_shader.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
index ea3d999e16c0364cf341d008eb8f398d5ec6777b..0ad8c523f7cb71156e520b5e0dbdf6526ce1baf5 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -6225,7 +6225,16 @@ iter_instruction(struct tgsi_iterate_context *iter,
          struct immed *imd = &ctx->imm[inst->Src[0].Register.Index];
          if (ctx->so && ctx->key->gs_present)
             emit_so_movs(ctx, &ctx->glsl_strbufs, &ctx->has_clipvertex_so);
-         if (ctx->cfg->has_cull_distance && ctx->key->gs.emit_clip_distance)
+         /* gs.emit_clip_distance only says whether the legacy user clip
+          * planes have to be evaluated here; that path lives inside
+          * emit_clip_dist_movs() and applies when the shader declares no
+          * clip or cull distance of its own. A shader that does declare
+          * them holds them in clip_dist_temp and has to publish them on
+          * every vertex it emits, whether or not a clip plane is enabled,
+          * because gl_CullDistance culls and gl_ClipDistance may be read
+          * by the fragment shader. */
+         if (ctx->cfg->has_cull_distance &&
+             (ctx->key->gs.emit_clip_distance || ctx->num_out_clip_dist))
             emit_clip_dist_movs(ctx, &ctx->glsl_strbufs);
          emit_prescale(&ctx->glsl_strbufs);
          if (imd->val[inst->Src[0].Register.SwizzleX].ui > 0) {
